  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "Given two positive integers aaa and bbb, calculate their product without using the multiplication operator.\n\n**Hint**: Use the Russian Peasant algorithm:\n\n\nInitialize result as 0\nWhile b is greater than 0:\n\nIf b is odd, add a to result\nDouble a\nHalve b (integer division)\n\n\nReturn the final result.\n\n\nInput Format\n\nFirst line contains TTT - number of test cases\nNext TTT lines each contain two space-separated integers aaa and bbb\n\n\nOutput Format\n\nFor each test case, output a single integer representing a×ba × ba×b calculated using Russian Peasant algorithm",
    "constraints": [],
    "inputFormat": "",
    "outputFormat": "",
    "notes": [],
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "2\n12 15\n20 7",
        "output": "180\n140",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nTest Case 1: (12, 15)\n\n15 is odd: result = 0 + 12 = 12\na = 24, b = 7\n7 is odd: result = 12 + 24 = 36\na = 48, b = 3\n3 is odd: result = 36 + 48 = 84\na = 96, b = 1\n1 is odd: result = 84 + 96 = 180\n\nTest Case 2: (20, 7)\n\n7 is odd: result = 0 + 20 = 20\na = 40, b = 3\n3 is odd: result = 20 + 40 = 60\na = 80, b = 1\n1 is odd: result = 60 + 80 = 140"
      }
    ]
  },
